  "grammar": [
    {
      "id": "b3_u01_l2_g1",
      "pattern": "A/V-(으)니까, N(이)니까",
      "meaning_uz": "...gani uchun, ... ekan (sabab)",
      "meaning_en": "Because / since (reason)",
      "explanation_md": "**-(으)니까** sababni bildiradi: \"...gani uchun\", \"... ekan, shuning uchun\". Ayniqsa **taklif yoki buyruqdan oldin** keladi.\n\n**주말이니까 미리 예약하세요.** — *Dam olish kuni ekan, oldindan band qiling.*\n\n### Qanday yasaladi\n\n- O'zak **받침siz** → **-니까**: 바쁘다 → **바쁘니까**, 빠르다 → **빠르니까**\n- O'zak **받침 bilan** → **-으니까**: 많다 → **많으니까**, 늦었다 → **늦었으니까**\n- **ㄹ** tushadi: 멀다 → **머니까**\n- **Ot** → **N(이)니까**: 주말 → **주말이니까**, 친구 → **친구니까**\n\n### -아서/어서 bilan farqi (2-kitob)\n\n- **-아서/어서** dan keyin **-(으)세요, -(으)ㄹ까요?** ishlatilmaydi: ~~늦어서 택시를 타세요~~\n- **-(으)니까** bilan mumkin: **늦으니까 택시를 타세요.** ✓",
      "explanation_md_en": "**-(으)니까** gives a reason: \"because\", \"since\". It's especially common **before a suggestion or a request**.\n\n**주말이니까 미리 예약하세요.** — *It's the weekend, so book in advance.*\n\n### How to form it\n\n- Stem **without 받침** → **-니까**: 바쁘다 → **바쁘니까**, 빠르다 → **빠르니까**\n- Stem **with 받침** → **-으니까**: 많다 → **많으니까**, 늦었다 → **늦었으니까**\n- **ㄹ** drops: 멀다 → **머니까**\n- **Noun** → **N(이)니까**: 주말 → **주말이니까**, 친구 → **친구니까**\n\n### vs -아서/어서 (book 2)\n\n- **-아서/어서** can't be followed by **-(으)세요** or **-(으)ㄹ까요?**: ~~늦어서 택시를 타세요~~\n- **-(으)니까** can: **늦으니까 택시를 타세요.** ✓",
      "formation": [
        {
          "condition_uz": "받침 yo'q",
          "condition_en": "No 받침",
          "rule": "A/V + 니까",
          "example": "바쁘니까, 빠르니까"
        },
        {
          "condition_uz": "받침 bor",
          "condition_en": "With 받침",
          "rule": "A/V + 으니까",
          "example": "많으니까, 있으니까"
        },
        {
          "condition_uz": "Ot",
          "condition_en": "Noun",
          "rule": "N(이)니까",
          "example": "주말이니까, 친구니까"
        }
      ],
      "examples": [
