    {
      "id": "b3_u01_l2_g2",
      "pattern": "V-(으)ㄹ게요",
      "meaning_uz": "...aman (va'da, o'z zimmasiga olish)",
      "meaning_en": "I'll … (promise, offer)",
      "explanation_md": "**-(으)ㄹ게요** — gapiruvchining **va'dasi yoki taklifi**: \"men ... qilaman\". Ko'pincha suhbatdoshga **yoqadigan** ish uchun.\n\n**제가 예약할게요.** — *Men band qilaman.*\n\n### Qanday yasaladi\n\n- O'zak **받침siz** → **-ㄹ게요**: 하다 → **할게요**, 가다 → **갈게요**\n- O'zak **받침 bilan** → **-을게요**: 찾다 → **찾을게요**, 맡다 → **맡을게요**\n- **ㄹ** bilan → **-게요**: 만들다 → **만들게요**\n- **돕다** → **도울게요**\n\n### Esda tuting\n\n- Faqat **\"men\"** (1-shaxs) uchun. ~~민지 씨가 할게요~~ emas.\n- So'roqda ishlatilmaydi: ~~할게요?~~ — o'rniga **-(으)ㄹ까요?**\n- **-(으)ㄹ 거예요** (reja) bilan farqi: **할게요** — suhbatdoshga va'da/taklif, **할 거예요** — oddiy reja haqida xabar.",
      "explanation_md_en": "**-(으)ㄹ게요** is the speaker's **promise or offer**: \"I'll …\". It's usually something that helps or considers the listener.\n\n**제가 예약할게요.** — *I'll make the reservation.*\n\n### How to form it\n\n- Stem **without 받침** → **-ㄹ게요**: 하다 → **할게요**, 가다 → **갈게요**\n- Stem **with 받침** → **-을게요**: 찾다 → **찾을게요**, 맡다 → **맡을게요**\n- **ㄹ** stem → **-게요**: 만들다 → **만들게요**\n- **돕다** → **도울게요**\n\n### Remember\n\n- Only for **\"I\"** (first person). Not ~~민지 씨가 할게요~~.\n- Not used in questions: not ~~할게요?~~ — use **-(으)ㄹ까요?**\n- vs **-(으)ㄹ 거예요** (plan): **할게요** is a promise/offer to the listener, **할 거예요** just states a plan.",
      "formation": [
        {
          "condition_uz": "받침 yo'q",
          "condition_en": "No 받침",
          "rule": "V + ㄹ게요",
          "example": "할게요, 갈게요, 연락할게요"
        },
        {
          "condition_uz": "받침 bor",
          "condition_en": "With 받침",
          "rule": "V + 을게요",
          "example": "찾을게요, 맡을게요"
        },
        {
          "condition_uz": "ㄹ bilan",
          "condition_en": "Ends in ㄹ",
          "rule": "V + 게요",
          "example": "만들게요"
        }
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "ko": "제가 예약할게요.",
          "uz": "Men band qilaman.",
          "en": "I'll make the reservation.",
          "audio": "b31b5b186c05.mp3"
        },
        {
          "ko": "도착하면 연락할게요.",
          "uz": "Yetib borsam, xabar beraman.",
          "en": "I'll let you know when I arrive.",
          "audio": "d3aca84d9fbe.mp3"
        },
        {
          "ko": "숙소는 제가 찾을게요.",
          "uz": "Turar joyni men topaman.",
          "en": "I'll find the accommodation.",
          "audio": "abe458f73562.mp3"
        },
        {
          "ko": "음식은 제가 만들게요.",
          "uz": "Ovqatni men tayyorlayman.",
          "en": "I'll make the food.",
          "audio": "33b4ae660bbc.mp3"
        },
        {
          "ko": "걱정하지 마세요. 제가 도울게요.",
          "uz": "Xavotir olmang, men yordam beraman.",
          "en": "Don't worry. I'll help.",
          "audio": "3254d0438f8e.mp3"
        }
      ],
      "mistakes": [
        {
          "wrong": "제가 찾을게요요.",
          "right": "제가 찾을게요.",
          "why_uz": "Bitta -요.",
          "why_en": "Only one -요."
        },
        {
          "wrong": "제가 예약할게요?",
          "right": "제가 예약할까요?",
          "why_uz": "So'roqda -(으)ㄹ까요?.",
          "why_en": "In questions use -(으)ㄹ까요?."
        },
        {
          "wrong": "음식은 제가 만들을게요.",
          "right": "음식은 제가 만들게요.",
          "why_uz": "ㄹ bilan tugasa: 만들게요.",
          "why_en": "ㄹ stems: 만들게요."
        }
      ],
      "uz_compare": "O'zbekchadagi va'da ohangidagi 'men qilaman!' ga mos: 'Men band qilaman' = 제가 예약할게요. Faqat o'zingiz haqingizda.",
      "compare_en": "Like English 'I'll …' when offering or promising: 'I'll book it' = 제가 예약할게요. Only for yourself, never in questions."
    }
  ],
  "dialogue": {
    "lines": [
      {
        "speaker": "minji",
        "ko": "아지즈 씨, 부산 여행 일정을 정해요.",
        "uz": "Aziz, Pusan sayohati jadvalini belgilaylik.",
        "en": "Aziz, let's set the schedule for the Busan trip.",
        "audio": "5b24a7b6413b.mp3"
      },
      {
        "speaker": "aziz",
        "ko": "좋아요. 금요일에 출발하는 게 어때요?",
        "uz": "Mayli. Juma kuni jo'nasak-chi?",
        "en": "Sure. How about leaving on Friday?",
        "audio": "0dda88db0a42.mp3"
      },
      {
        "speaker": "minji",
        "ko": "금요일은 수업이 있으니까 토요일에 가요.",
        "uz": "Juma kuni darsim bor, shanba kuni boraylik.",
        "en": "I have class on Friday, so let's go on Saturday.",
        "audio": "664ac7c29b3e.mp3"
      },
      {
        "speaker": "aziz",
        "ko": "알겠어요. 그럼 기차표는 제가 예약할게요.",
        "uz": "Xo'p. Unda poyezd chiptasini men band qilaman.",
        "en": "Okay. Then I'll book the train tickets.",
        "audio": "80d4b8ee4011.mp3"
      },
      {
        "speaker": "minji",
        "ko": "주말이니까 표가 없을 거예요. 오늘 예약하세요.",
        "uz": "Dam olish kuni, chipta qolmasligi mumkin. Bugun band qiling.",
        "en": "It's the weekend, so tickets may run out. Book today.",
        "audio": "5e66d6a617e5.mp3"
      },
      {
        "speaker": "aziz",
        "ko": "네, 지금 바로 할게요. 숙소는 어떻게 해요?",
        "uz": "Xo'p, hoziroq qilaman. Turar joy-chi?",
        "en": "Sure, I'll do it right now. What about accommodation?",
        "audio": "3e925bbfb3ad.mp3"
      },
      {
        "speaker": "minji",
        "ko": "숙소는 제가 찾을게요. 게스트하우스가 싸니까 거기로 해요.",
        "uz": "Turar joyni men topaman. Mehmon uyi arzon, o'shani olaylik.",
        "en": "I'll find a place. Guesthouses are cheap, so let's stay at one.",
        "audio": "8af924ecaaca.mp3"
      },
      {
        "speaker": "aziz",
        "ko": "좋아요. 바다 근처에 있으면 좋겠어요.",
        "uz": "Yaxshi. Dengizga yaqin bo'lsa yaxshi bo'lardi.",
        "en": "Good. It'd be nice if it's near the sea.",
        "audio": "58ee2879356f.mp3"
      },
      {
        "speaker": "minji",
        "ko": "알아볼게요. 짐은 많지 않으니까 가방 하나만 가져가요.",
        "uz": "Surishtiraman. Yuk ko'p emas, bitta sumka olamiz.",
        "en": "I'll look into it. We won't have much, so let's bring one bag each.",
        "audio": "7497135e2c40.mp3"
      },
      {
        "speaker": "aziz",
        "ko": "네. 예약하면 바로 연락할게요.",
        "uz": "Xo'p. Band qilsam, darhol xabar beraman.",
        "en": "Okay. I'll let you know as soon as I've booked.",
        "audio": "140f24957667.mp3"
      },
      {
        "speaker": "minji",
        "ko": "고마워요. 꼭 창가 자리로 해 주세요!",
        "uz": "Rahmat. Albatta deraza yonidagi joyni oling!",
        "en": "Thanks. Make sure you get window seats!",
        "audio": "bf6cba6c5045.mp3"
      }
    ]
  },
